complex character.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:48.835
Someone who was dealing with
huge philosophical questions

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you know, waiting fo
his mother to die,

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:52.739 line:92%
for his life to take meaning

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.508
Suddenly, it was like, "Oh, he's
not just a kind of prince.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:03:01.314
This is a kind of -- this is
Shakespearean in its quality

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
So yeah, I got really excite
once I spoke to them.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.987
In terms of my experience with
the Royal Family, I'm the wors

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
person to talk about
the Royals.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.625
I have no idea about anything to
do with the Royal Family.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.260
-But I think that must be one of
the most fascinating

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.529
things about anyone who is
making this show right now

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:19.098
about a family that is obviously
still around,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I have to imagine,
especially when you're doing

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
press for the show, how ofte
people ask you your take

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.576
on the current things that are
