00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:34.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
be they new babies
or, you know, big interviews

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you just constantly let
people down by having

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
no interest or awareness?
-Oh, completely.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:43.489
I mean, I remember going to --
We went to the Golden Globes

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.292 line:92%
pre-lockdown, pre-pandemic

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:50.396
Went to the Golden Globes an
I was kind of -- I was wide-eyed

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
in sort of -- in amazement o
the whole thing.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:57.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the first time I'd been
to a major awards ceremony

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.106
And I remember going and we were
doing the press line,

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
Helena Bonham Carter, myself
and Erin Doherty,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.045 size:88% position:44% line:92%
who plays Princess Anne,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were going through
and every journalist

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:12.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
was asking us about Harry an
Meghan at the time.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
They always ask us about Harry
and Meghan,

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this was about Harry
and Meghan,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it came to me,
and I honestly was --

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
I felt such embarrassment at
knowing honestly nothing.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:27.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, really, it did tak
a moment to go,

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.002 line:92%
"Who is Harry and Meghan?"

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.703 line:92%
And then I realized who it was

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I'm the worst person."

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:36.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I sort of -- there couldn't
be a kind of less qualifie

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:40.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
spokesperson for
the Royal Family than me.

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it must make it nicer, to
some degree, to not have

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
that baggage when you play
a part,

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
because then you can play it
like a character

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.357
as opposed to, you know, havin
some -- the haunting image o

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
the real person sort of
lurking over you.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.094 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah. Oh, for sure.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think this is something that
I'm sort of --

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.466 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I've talked about a lot.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:06.539
I always think that I've never
played a real person before.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.874
But I remember when I was coming
to this,

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.642
there was a big kind of --
you know, because we'd had

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
season 1 and 2, and Claire Foy
and Matt Smith,

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are unbelievable in playin
the Queen and Phillip,

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:21.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had this huge pressure to
replicate

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.622 size:88% position:44% line:92%
the real Prince Charles.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:26.392
And so did I lots of work on
the voice and lots of work

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:30.263
on the way he stands and
the way his back is arched

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.030 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and all these things.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
And actually, it took seeing a
Todd Haynes film --

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.970 size:75% position:38%
the Todd Haynes film
about Bob Dylan --

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make me realize that
actually, you don't need t

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.176 line:92%
play the real person at all.

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that film,
if anyone's seen it --

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you've seen it
but it's beautiful.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:48.614 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, it's fantastic.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-8 actors playing, like,
not just Dylan

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, like aspects of
his personality.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, Heath Ledger play
the sort of, like,

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.256 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
rock star version,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:06:01.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Cate Blanchett plays
the most kind of recognizabl

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.261 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
version of Dylan.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I loved about it is rathe
than going, "Let's try and

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:08.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
imitate the real Dylan, becaus
none of us know who he is,

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
let's try and grapple with
the poetry

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.305 line:92%
and the essence of someone."

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, for me, it was reall
liberating knowing

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I don't know anything
about Charles,

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I could never
do a good version of him.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:23.249 line:92%
But also, I'm not a mimic.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:26.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, that was -- Yeah,
I found that really liberating

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:29.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
just going, "I'm just going to
play him for who he is."

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:33.693
For the kind of the essence of
him rather than the real person.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:35.161 line:92%
-Well, the approach paid off

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really a wonderful
portrayal,

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thanks so much for
being here.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a big fan,
and hopefully next time,

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can be here in person.
-Yeah, I hope so.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for having me
-Of course.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:48.141
The fourth season of "The Crown"
is streaming on Netflix.

